# Ad-hoc: Read Microsoft 365 Copilot enterprise interaction history
#
# This file resolves the signed-in user's ID, then calls:
#
# GET https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/copilot/users/{userId}/interactionHistory/getAllEnterpriseInteractions
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Important authorization boundary:
# - GET /me uses a delegated User.Read token only to resolve your own user ID.
# - getAllEnterpriseInteractions does not support delegated permissions.
# - The token request uses a separate confidential application.
# - The history request requires an application token with the
#   AiEnterpriseInteraction.Read.All application permission and admin consent.
# - Targeting your own user ID does not remove the application-permission
#   requirement.
#
# The target user needs a valid Microsoft 365 Copilot license with the
# Microsoft Copilot with Graph-grounded chat service plan.
#
# Manually put these values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id-used-for-browser-sign-in>
# A365_ENTERPRISE_INTERACTIONS_APP_CLIENT_ID=<confidential-app-client-id>
# A365_ENTERPRISE_INTERACTIONS_APP_CLIENT_SECRET_URLENCODED=<URL-encoded-secret>
#
# Use the client secret value, not its secret ID. URL-encode the complete value
# before writing it to .env so characters such as +, &, =, or % cannot change
# the form body. Keep .env ignored and remove the secret after the experiment.
#
# The token response is sensitive and short-lived. Do not save its response.
# Clear REST Client request history after the experiment because both the
# client secret request and access-token response may remain in local history.
#
# The response can contain user prompts, Copilot responses, meeting and file
# references, URLs, participant identifiers, and other confidential data.
# Do not commit, paste into chat or an issue, or capture identifying
# screenshots. Save any required raw response only under the ignored evidence
# directory.
#
# Evidence directory:
# ../../evidence/experiments/05-enterprise-interaction-history/
#
@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@applicationClientId = {{$dotenv A365_ENTERPRISE_INTERACTIONS_APP_CLIENT_ID}}
@applicationClientSecretUrlEncoded = {{$dotenv A365_ENTERPRISE_INTERACTIONS_APP_CLIENT_SECRET_URLENCODED}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@delegatedUserScope = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1 - Request a delegated device code
#
# Never save this response.

# @name interactionHistoryStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{delegatedUserScope}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Exchange the device code after browser sign-in
#
# Never save this response.

# @name interactionHistoryDelegatedToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{interactionHistoryStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.3 - Resolve your own Microsoft Entra user ID
#
# Keep the returned ID private. The next request uses only the ID from this
# named response; no user ID needs to be copied into the tracked file.
# Never save this response.

# @name interactionHistoryCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{interactionHistoryDelegatedToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 2 - Acquire the app-only Microsoft Graph token
#
# Before sending:
# - configure AiEnterpriseInteraction.Read.All as an application permission on
#   A365_ENTERPRISE_INTERACTIONS_APP_CLIENT_ID;
# - grant tenant admin consent; and
# - manually add the confidential app client ID and URL-encoded client secret
#   to the shared ignored ../../.env file.
#
# Expected: 200 with token_type Bearer and an access_token.
# Do not save or share the response.

# @name acquireEnterpriseInteractionsAppToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

client_id={{applicationClientId}}&client_secret={{applicationClientSecretUrlEncoded}}&scope=https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2F.default&grant_type=client_credentials

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3 - Get all enterprise interactions for the signed-in user
#
# This is the requested beta request. It uses the app-only token from the
# Part 2 response, not the delegated token from Part 1.
#
# Expected when authorized and licensed: 200 with a collection of
# aiInteraction objects.
#
# Interpret common failures carefully:
# - 401: token missing, malformed, or expired.
# - 403: application permission/admin consent/license or another authorization
#   requirement is not satisfied.
# - 404: do not conclude that the user has no interactions; record the exact
#   safe error class and recheck the target ID and endpoint availability.
#
# If @odata.nextLink is present, follow one page at a time using the URL
# returned by Graph. Do not publish that URL because it can contain sensitive
# query state.
#
# Save the first response as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/05-enterprise-interaction-history/beta-interactions-page-1.json
#
# If @odata.nextLink is present, save later pages as
# beta-interactions-page-2.json, beta-interactions-page-3.json, and so on in
# the same ignored evidence directory.

# @name getMyEnterpriseInteractionsBeta
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/users/{{interactionHistoryCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}/interactionHistory/getAllEnterpriseInteractions
Authorization: Bearer {{acquireEnterpriseInteractionsAppToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 4 - OPTIONAL documented v1.0 comparison
#
# Microsoft currently documents both beta and v1.0. Use this only when a
# stable-version comparison is useful. The recommended page size is 100.
#
# If sent, save the first response as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/05-enterprise-interaction-history/v1-interactions-page-1.json
#
# Save any later pages as v1-interactions-page-2.json and so on.

# @name getMyEnterpriseInteractionsV1
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/users/{{interactionHistoryCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}/interactionHistory/getAllEnterpriseInteractions?$top=100
Authorization: Bearer {{acquireEnterpriseInteractionsAppToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
